# This project's integrity model is content hashing: results/artifact_manifest.json
# and results/smoke_environment.json record SHA-256 digests of committed files,
# and configs are pinned by digest inside every measurement artifact.
#
# Git's end-of-line translation breaks that. With core.autocrlf=true, a Windows
# checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, so the same commit produces different bytes on
# different machines and every recorded digest fails away from the machine that
# wrote it. CI caught exactly this.
#
# Normalise to LF in the working tree on every platform so a digest means the
# same thing everywhere.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Evidence files: never translated, under any local setting.
results/*.json   -text
configs/*.json   -text
*.lock           -text

# Genuinely binary.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.safetensors binary
